From 24ed9108df7775425eaad8bbd1588e6bdb14fdf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 19:08:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] qmicli,loc: expose the constellation control messages

  --loc-get-constellation-control
  --loc-set-constellation-control=[reset|disabled-mask[,enabled-mask]]
  --loc-set-gnss-constellation-report-config=[measurement-mask[,polynomial-mask]]

The query prints the two constellation sets through the new adapter rather
than six separate lookups, and then the raw state values as well, so the
reply is not hidden behind an interpretation of an enumeration nobody has
published.

The masks taken by the setters are accepted verbatim, in any base, and are
described as opaque on purpose: their bit order is not the same in every
message and has not been established for all of them.

Like the rest of LOC, these are request-plus-indication: the response only
carries the generic result, and the real answer arrives in a later
indication. Reading the response alone tells you nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
